==English==
[[Image:Hoookah.jpg|thumb|right|200 px|A hookah.]]

===Etymology===
Urdu {{ur-Arab|[[حقہ]]}} < Arabic {{Arab|[[حقة]]}} (ħúqqa), meaning [[pot]], [[jar]] < {{Arab|[[حق]]}} (ħuqq), [[cavity]], [[hollow]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a [[pipe]] with a long flexible tube that draws the [[smoke]] through [[water]]. Originally invented in India, it gained most popularity in the Arab world. It is traditionally used for smoking tobacco, which is often flavored.

====Synonyms====
* [[hubble-bubble]]
* [[hubbly]]
* [[hubbly-bubbly]], [[hubbly bubbly]]
* [[narghile]]
* [[nargila]]
* [[sheesha]]
* [[shisha]]

